11.	O @wDN{An}, strengthen the foundations of the throne of life. 
12.	@wRN{Rīm-@wDN{Sîn}}, 
13.	may your name be called by a name of life; 
14.	may he look upon you with favourable eyes, 
15.	and pay attention to you. 
$ (@gap{1 line unclear}) 
17.	May he determine a destiny of life as a fate for you. 
18.	@wRN{Rīm-@wDN{Sîn}}, may you be beloved of @wDN{An}, and may your kingship endure forever. 
19.	Great @wDN{An}, make him shepherd of the numerous people. 
